q q .121569 .227451 .372549 RG 1.2 w 25.51181 25.51181 544.25198 790.8661 re S .717647 .768627 .819608 RG .5 w 34.01575 34.01575 527.2441 773.8583 re S .121569 .227451 .372549 rg BT 10.2 TL/F2 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 39.68504 802.2047 Tm T* ET .333333 .333333 .333333 rg BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 477.3186 802.2047 Tm (RegNo: )Tj T* ET 39.68504 793.7008 m 555.5906 793.7008 l S .4 .4 .4 rg BT 9 TL/F1 7.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 39.68504 39.68504 Tm <507974686f6e20436f6e766572736174696f6e616c204c6f6f7020972052756c652d42617365642043686174626f74>Tj T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 531.8231 39.68504 Tm (Page 2)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 753.5276 cm .121569 .227451 .372549 rg BT 20 TL/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (2. Complete Python Implementation)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 700.5276 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 34.5 Tm (The following program is written specifically for this task. It keeps the logic simple enough to)Tj T* (understand and demonstrate, while adding enough conversational cases to show that the chatbot is)Tj T* (more than a two-response example.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 298.3276 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 10.4 TL/F5 8.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 386.9 Tm (# Rule-Based Python Chatbot)Tj T* (# Student: )Tj T* (# RegNo: )Tj T* T* (print\("=== Welcome to )Tj[-5399.9997]TJ ( Rule-Based Chatbot ==="\))Tj T* (name = input\("Before we begin, what is your name? "\).strip\(\))Tj T* T* (print\(f"Hello, {name}! I am a simple rule-based chatbot."\))Tj T* (print\("You can ask me about Python, my capabilities, or how I am."\))Tj T* (print\("Type 'bye' or 'exit' whenever you want to end the conversation.\\n"\))Tj T* T* (while True:)Tj T* (    user_input = input\(f"{name}: "\).lower\(\).strip\(\))Tj T* T* (    if "bye" in user_input or "exit" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: Goodbye! It was nice talking with you."\))Tj T* (        break)Tj T* T* (    elif "hello" in user_input or "hi" in user_input or "hey" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\(f"Bot: Hello, {name}! Nice to meet you. How can I help you today?"\))Tj T* T* (    elif "how are you" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: I'm doing great! Thanks for asking. I'm ready to help."\))Tj T* T* (    elif "what is python" in user_input or "python" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: Python is a high-level programming language known for its clear syntax and wide range of applications."\))Tj T* T* (    elif "what can you do" in user_input or "help" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: I can answer basic questions about Python, learning, and general topics. Try asking me something!"\))Tj T* T* (    elif "time" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: I cannot access the live clock, but you can check the current time on your device."\))Tj T* T* (    elif "thank" in user_input:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: You're welcome! I'm glad I could help."\))Tj T* T* (    else:)Tj T* (        print\("Bot: I'm not sure I understand that yet. Try asking about Python, my capabilities, or how I am."\))Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 263.1543 cm .14902 .196078 .219608 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Why this implementation is robust)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 62.69291 197.1543 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm (The exit condition is checked before the other conversational rules, so the user can always leave the)Tj T* (program. Greeting detection uses the )Tj/F2 10.5 Tf (in)Tj/F1 10.5 Tf ( operator rather than exact equality, which handles phrases)Tj T* (containing a greeting. The remaining branches cover multiple topics, and the final )Tj/F2 10.5 Tf (else)Tj/F1 10.5 Tf ( gives a useful)Tj T* (recovery response instead of failing silently.)Tj T* ET Q Q

